physical.summary:
(Steinhauer description for As.St.895.a-c)
&quot;3-5. Three poisoned arrows which the Dayaks commonly blow through the shaft of their spears; some of them however have blowpipes. The poison here used is called &#039;Upos&#039;, probably the Javanese &#039;Upas&#039;.&quot;
Christy slip reads: &quot;They are 10-11 inches long made of a slender strip of bamboo rind or reed. Two of them have expanded blades. A conical piece of soft pith is placed on their butts.&quot;

